<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged into the generated Info.plist at bundle time. Tauri looks for this
  file by name, in the same directory as tauri.conf.json, with no configuration
  needed (tauri-utils 2.9.3, MacConfig::info_plist).

  A separate file and not a key in tauri.conf.json because Tauri offers no
  inline form: the only alternatives are this or a path to somewhere else,
  which would be the same file further away.

  Only two keys, and both are load-bearing.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Without this key macOS does not show a microphone prompt and deny it — it
    kills the process, on the first frame cpal asks for. An app whose entire
    purpose is listening cannot ship without it, and it fails at exactly the
    moment nothing has been logged yet.

    The wording is what the user reads in the system dialog, so it says where
    the audio goes rather than what the app is. "Never leaves this computer" is
    the fact that matters to someone being asked for their microphone, and it
    is true: the model runs locally and there is no network path after the
    first-run download.
  -->
  <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Kotha listens when you press the dictation key, and transcribes what you say on this computer. Your voice never leaves it.</string>

  <!--
    An agent app: no Dock icon, no ⌘-Tab entry, driven by the menu bar and a
    hotkey. `setup` sets the same thing at runtime with
    ActivationPolicy::Accessory; this sets it from launch, which is the
    difference between no Dock icon and a Dock icon that appears and vanishes.

    It does not stop the first-run window taking focus — an agent app may
    activate itself when it asks, which is what tao's set_focus does.

    If that window ever fails to come forward, this is the line to try
    removing first: the runtime call still covers the pill.
  -->
  <key>LSUIElement</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
